{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe code-review thresholds in force were adjudicated on the **code-v3** corpus. `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION`\nmoved to **code-v5** on 2026-08-21 (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py:35`), one day before the\nlast routing flip. ADR 0036 forbids pooling across impact-model versions, so every committed\nthreshold was tuned against a model that is no longer running, and ~1,100 code-v5 sidecars accrued\nunanalysed. This ticket runs that segmented replay, LANDS IT AS AN IN-TREE RECORD, and applies the\ntwo flips it clears.\n\nIt also repairs the generator, which could not produce a trustworthy replay: CORRECTION (E) in\n`docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` records that\n`calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py` reads no routing index, so every re-run reproduces two\nknown-wrong rows (`sec` reported as a DET/attestation gate; `project.review-phase-boundaries`\nreported at 0.95 rather than the 0.90 the project overlay sets). Fixing it was deferred there.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. `docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py` — read routing + label synonyms through\n   the production path (`registry.effective_routing`, `registry.normalize_criteria`) with a\n   pure-JSON fallback; identify DET criteria by routing `exec` rather than a validity heuristic;\n   default `--impact-model-version` to the version the gate stamps today rather than a hardcoded\n   `code-v3`; print proposals as a DELTA against committed routing; add\n   `--dump-newly-blocking CRIT=THR`.\n2. `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` — mark CORRECTION (E) resolved.\n3. `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md` — NEW. The calibration-4\n   record: corpus, method, the per-flip adjudication, the rejected severity floor, the\n   zero-impact analysis, and the friction table. This is the artifact the routing `_comment`s\n   cite, mirroring how the `api-compat` and `tests` entries cite their own calibration source.\n4. `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` — two entries only:\n   - `security`: `block_threshold` 0.54 -> 0.45 (stays `blocking_enabled: true`).\n   - `concurrency`: `default_posture` advisory -> blocking, `block_threshold` 0.95 -> 0.52,\n     `blocking_enabled` false -> true.\n   Each gains an `_comment` naming ticket `3055-e92d-7063-4a32` and the new record's path.\n5. `tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py` — `DERIVED_THRESHOLD` 0.54 -> 0.45, and the\n   nit-band assertion `_blocks([\"security\"], 0.50) is False` must move below the new line (0.50\n   now blocks; 0.40 is the new \"just under\" probe). The test's intent — a low-priority nit does\n   not block — is preserved, re-anchored to the new threshold.\n6. `tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py` — two edits:\n   - `test_replay_script_advertises_the_routed_blocking_set` asserts the advertised set is\n     disjoint from `{\"docs\", \"concurrency\", \"scope-intent\", \"maintainability\"}`; drop\n     `concurrency` from that literal. (`blocking_set()` itself derives from the routing index,\n     so the loop above it self-updates.)\n   - `test_document_decision_column_matches_the_routed_posture` currently admits only `flip`\n     and `hold` and `pytest.fail`s on anything else. The code-v4 table's\n     `| concurrency | 0.54 | ... | hold |` row is a HISTORICAL record of a measurement taken\n     over the code-v3 corpus and must not be rewritten to say `flip` — that would misreport\n     what code-v4 measured. Add a third decision word `superseded`, and assert that a\n     `superseded` row names the later record that governs it. This keeps both artifacts\n     honest: the old table still says what it measured, and the test still binds the routing\n     to *some* record.\n7. `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` — besides marking CORRECTION (E)\n   resolved, change the code-v4 replay table's `concurrency` decision cell from `hold` to\n   `superseded` with a pointer to the code-v5 record, and add one sentence under the table\n   stating the hold reason (n=1, below `MIN_N = 25`) expired when the code-v5 segment gave it\n   n=68.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAdjudication reads the findings each flip would newly block (priority in\n`[proposed, current)`), classifying each TP-blockworthy / TP-but-nit / FP against the source tree.\nFull detail, including the counts and the per-finding basis, lands in the record added by item 3.\n\n- `security` @0.45: 13 newly-blocking, 13 TP-blockworthy, 0 nit, 0 FP. Friction 0.29% -> 1.43%\n  of 703 changes. Mean validity 0.990; zero findings below validity 0.5.\n- `concurrency` @0.52: 2 newly-blocking, both TP-blockworthy, 0 nit, 0 FP. Friction 0.29%. Held\n  advisory previously only because n=1 was below the script's `MIN_N = 25` floor; code-v5 gives\n  n=68 (53 surviving). 0.52 not 0.50 because the three adjudicated nits sit at priority 0.5143,\n  and because `threshold_for` resolves multi-criterion findings at the MIN of their thresholds,\n  so 0.52 limits the leak onto co-tagged `correctness` (blocking@0.54) to 0.02.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Routing `maintainability` (53% of what it would block is nit or FP; deferred pending a separator).\n- Any change to `impact_code`. A `blast_radius`/`debt_impact` floor was measured and REJECTED —\n  44% of the 48 findings it would newly block were nits or FPs. The record states the evidence.\n- The `supply-chain` / `scope-intent` prompt remediations.\n\n## Back-out\n\nReverting the two JSON entries to their prior values (`security` 0.54; `concurrency` 0.95 /\nadvisory / `blocking_enabled: false`) is the rollback path; no data migration is involved.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `security` is routed at 0.45 and still blocking.\n      Oracle: `python -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json'));assert d['security']['block_threshold']==0.45 and d['security']['blocking_enabled'] is True\"`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] `concurrency` is routed blocking at 0.52.\n      Oracle: `python -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json'));c=d['concurrency'];assert c['block_threshold']==0.52 and c['blocking_enabled'] is True and c['default_posture']=='blocking'\"`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] Both entries cite this ticket by its canonical id.\n      Oracle: `grep -c \"3055-e92d-7063-4a32\" src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`\n      returns >= 2.\n- [ ] No other criterion's posture or threshold changes.\n      Oracle: `git diff src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` shows changed lines only\n      inside the `security` and `concurrency` objects.\n- [ ] The calibration record exists and is cited by the routing comments.\n      Oracle: `test -f docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md` exits 0, and\n      `grep -c \"code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5\" src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`\n      returns >= 2.\n- [ ] The generator is routing-aware: on the code-v3 segment it emits no `sec` row and no\n      `documentation` row (both normalize into `security` / `docs`), and reports\n      `project.review-phase-boundaries` at its overlay threshold 0.90.\n      Oracle: `python docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py --tracker <checkout>/.tickets-tracker --impact-model-version code-v3`\n      output has no line beginning `sec ` or `documentation `, and its\n      `project.review-phase-boundaries` row shows `adv@0.90`.\n- [ ] CORRECTION (E) in `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` is marked resolved.\n      Oracle: `grep -c \"CORRECTION (E) — RESOLVED\" docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md`\n      returns 1.\n- [ ] The tests that pinned the old posture are updated, not deleted, and still assert their\n      original intent.\n      Oracle: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py -q`\n      exits 0, and `git diff --stat tests/unit/test_code_review_blocking_replay.py` shows a\n      modification (not a deletion), with a test named for the nit band still present.\n- [ ] The code-v4 replay table still records what code-v4 measured.\n      Oracle: `grep -n \"| concurrency | 0.54 |\" docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md`\n      still matches, and its decision cell reads `superseded`, not `flip`.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change is MERGED (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788906545279526001,"uuid":"4f2b2c72-bf69-4fb5-a933-ab2ab665c90a"}